+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` validates incoming tool arguments against each registered tool's `inputSchema` before invoking its executor. A rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` describing the schema failure so the model can correct its arguments on the next round of the orchestrator loop, while only an unregistered tool name throws.
+
+## Registration and Compilation
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` immediately so an uncompilable schema fails at registration time with an error naming the tool ([validated by: throws at registration when a static inputSchema fails to compile, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration rather than recompiled on every `execute` call ([validated by: compiles a static tool schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L96)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves and validates against the schema current at that `execute` call, passing valid inputs and unlisted extra properties through to the executor unchanged ([validated by: validates dynamic tool definitions against the current schema and passes unlisted properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+
+## Execution and Rejection Behaviour
+
+- When input violates the resolved `inputSchema`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and expected constraint without invoking the executor, and never writes or returns raw input values ([validated by: rejects schema-invalid input without calling the executor and without leaking input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L26)).
+- Within `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`, a rejected tool call is returned as a `tool_result` message to the model so the orchestrator tool loop can recover on a subsequent round without throwing ([validated by: returns a validation rejection to the model so the orchestrator tool loop can retry and resolve](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L133)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared JSON Schema types, and `enum` without stripping unlisted properties, applying schema defaults, or coercing values.
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when called with an unregistered tool name.
